cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this experimental data or code, please cite it as below."
title: "Quantum Space Memory v2: 2-Stage IBM Heron Zeno Validation and Cross-Chip Blind Demodulator Audit"
authors:
  - family-names: "Máté"
    given-names: "Róbert"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-3986-6039"
date-released: 2026-11-09
version: 2.0.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/silentnoisehun/quantum-space-memory-v2"
license: "MIT"
keywords:
  - "quantum-computing"
  - "quantum-zeno-effect"
  - "ibm-heron"
  - "qiskit"
  - "blind-decoder"
  - "null-hypothesis"
abstract: >-
  Pre-registered, two-stage physical quantum memory evaluation on 156-qubit IBM Heron
  superconducting processors (ibm_marrakesh and ibm_kingston). Stage 1 independently
  verified quantum Zeno population pinning (+98.44 pp in B0, +82.95 pp in B3) and Bell
  parity mixing (+45.95 pp). Stage 2 executed a pre-registered 16-frequency blind spectral
  periodogram detector on raw complex128 kerneled IQ heterodyne demodulation data, confirming
  the exact null result (P_max = 4.98 < E[noise] = 6.53, p_family = 0.93, coupling < 14.36%).
